I'm planning to do a live workshop and demonstration of installing SE Linux
at an upcoming CASEL user group meeting.

I know the NSA kernel was developed in parallel with Red Hat Linux and that
another version is available for Debian.  I plan to do a workshop on either
installing the Red Hat version on a Dell and another one installing with the
Debian version on a Power Macintosh.  Does anyone have a preference as to
which is conducted first?

Are there any "lessons learned" I should be aware of with the Debian
version?  I'm under the impression that it is less mature than the Red Hat
version.

